<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Salomon cuts Thyssen to hold.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Salomon cuts Thyssen to hold.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Bros said on Wednesday it cut German steelmaker Thyssen to hold from buy. In a research note, analyst Terence Sinclair said there were opportunities for further gains in the stock but a lot of the expected gains from restructuring were already reflected in its share price.</p>
<p>He said he continued to be bullish on European steel volumes and prices and expected prices to firm through the yend of the year.</p>
<p>However Salomon's target of 410 marks on Thyssen shares did not offer much upside, he said.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
